load_theory — implementation plan
==================================

status: done (2026-07-10)

wave 2: SCALA-side tool — no MCP.ir involved. backing decision (spec
"theory loading and checking"): scala use_theories and ML Thy_Info are
disjoint registries; load/check live on the scala side, and
Ir.load_theory's headless refusal (Printer.show_markup_default) is
KEPT — the "load_theory" fname stays in the dispatcher but the builtin
tool never calls it. references I3 (builtin table) only; I1/I2 do not
apply.

advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          load_theory
description   "Load and check a theory from disk (with its transitive
              dependencies) into the running session, by
              session-qualified long name (\"HOL-Library.Multiset\")
              or by path via master_dir. After loading, the theory is
              'loaded' tier: source, commands, diagnostics and
              entities resources answer live, repl_init_from_source
              can attach to it, and it is auto-added to the resource
              scope. Replies with per-theory ok/error status;
              errors carry positions. Loading is the expensive
              promotion — a deep import chain outside the base image
              can take minutes; see list_theories for what is already
              available."
              (source: mcp_server.py load_theory :426 + the spec's
              tier/promotion story.)
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "name": {"type": "string"},
                 "master_dir": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["name"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": false, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}
              (mutating per the spec blanket — it changes session
              state and scope. idempotent: re-loading an unchanged
              theory is a no-op at the document level.)
outputSchema  none.

name/argument mapping across the layers
---------------------------------------

  mcp client edge   tools/call "load_theory",
                    {"name": "HOL-Library.Multiset"}
  scala builtin row handler calls MCP_Session.load_theory (NEW) —
                    no bridge, no fname. json -> plain scala args.
  scala method      resolve the name through the startup
                    Sessions.load_structure/deps path map (session-
                    qualified names work without a master_dir);
                    session.use_theories(...); collect per-node
                    status + messages (template:
                    Server_Commands.Use_Theories); auto-add to scope
                    (wave 4 — no-op stub until scope exists).
  engine            none (PIDE document processing).

implementation steps
--------------------

1. [infra, shared with check_theory/unload_theory] MCP_Session.
   load_theory(name, master_dir?): use_theories + diagnostics
   extraction into (ok, text-with-positions). mcp_session.scala
   already runs use_theories at startup for the -T theory — factor
   that call so both paths share it.
2. [infra, shared with wave 3] keep the Sessions.load_structure +
   deps object from startup; name -> path/session resolution.
3. [this tool] builtin row + handler; per-node errors -> isError
   result carrying the diagnostics text (an error REPLY is still the
   full report — the model needs the positions).
4. tests.

