T1  use_theories on a well-formed .thy under a master_dir loads it
    and reports ok; the theory is then visible to
    repl_init_from_source (snapshot exists).
    test [bridge/scala-integration, mcp_test -b]: load a small
    fixture theory (mcp/test/), assert ok + node status.
T2  a broken theory yields isError with line-positioned messages,
    and the session survives (next load works).
    test [bridge]: fixture with a bad lemma -> error text contains
    the line; load the good fixture after -> ok.
T3  session-qualified names resolve without master_dir via the
