T4  re-loading an unchanged theory is fast and ok (idempotency
    claim); re-loading after a disk edit picks up the new content
    (this is check_theory's core, shared fixture).
    test [bridge]: load, load again -> both ok.
T5  scope auto-add fires once scope exists (wave 4); until then the
    stub is a recorded no-op.
    test [scala unit, deferred to plans/scope_add]: load_theory then
    scope_show contains the theory.
T6  full chain.
    test [e2e]: load fixture -> read
    isabelle://theory/{name}/diagnostics? (resource, separate plan)
    -> repl_init_from_source attach (plans/repl_init_from_source T5).

